Z||000000||foxgapfiero||11-03-2001||04:34 PM||||I'd like to start mailing with anyone that has built a Fiero trailer. Even if you have one but didn't build it yourself. I have the doner car just about ready to cut but need some ideas from people that allready have done it. Have you used the original suspension? Did you cut a coil on the springs  to bring it to the correct height without the engine? Did you say the heck with it and used a light trailer suspension? Did you leave the rear clip in place for a type of wing? Did you cut the clip off flush with the deck lid? I've got lots of other questions and will appreciate lots of people to answer them or at least give their opinions. Skitime  sent me some great photos a while back but more can't hurt. Thanks in advance to all who reply.  <P>------------------<BR>Mark Hoagland<BR>86GT 3.4<BR>88GT T-Top<BR>85GT caddy v-8 next swap<BR>84SE trailer next project||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||11-03-2001||05:38 PM||||the neatest one I seen had the first few feet molded onto the last few feet. made half the hood and half the engine cover made into one lift up lid. I think they used stock rear cradle/suspension.||||reg||1
